       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses are:\n- **50 mg once daily**, a common starting dose for depression or anxiety.\n- **100 mg or 200 mg once daily**, for titration to a higher dose. 200 mg is the ceiling.\n- **Another dose or drug**, if you meant something different.\n\nPlease confirm the dose with your supervising resident or attending. Once you have the right dose, tell me and I'll enter it right away. If the high dose is intentional, for example on the advice of a psychiatry consultant, tell me. I'd still suggest getting that documented and verified by pharmacy before I enter it."
      }
